STILL RECORDING, tape 11: "Store 214" (2026). Halloway Archive. Original story, pictures, sound and music. A work of fiction.

Pictures: drawn in code (canvas 2D) with the tape kit (channel/brand/tapekit.js): a 2.5D renderer, CCTV grading, the handheld camcorder look and VHS damage. The upper level at store 214, its roll-down grille, and the four mannequins (built in 3D from tapered bodies swept along curved spines, jointed at the neck, shoulders and elbows) are drawn for this tape (film.js).
Fonts: VT323 (The VT323 Project Authors), SIL Open Font License 1.1. Special Elite (Astigmatic), Apache License 2.0.
Voice: ElevenLabs text-to-speech, model eleven_v4. Leon Marsh: "HA Leon Marsh" (ElevenLabs Voice Design, made for this series).
Sound effects: generated with ElevenLabs Sound Effects (prompts in sfx/prompts.json).
Music: none. A low drone made from the mall's own ventilation (tools/score.py).
Sound: every sound is at the storefront and is heard through Leon's camcorder or CAM 31 (tools/mix.py: rooms, the camcorder's automatic level control, the tape).
